# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Mojtaba Haghighatlari et al. (2022). NewtonNet: a Newtonian message passing network for deep learning of interatomic potentials and forces.
#   Digital Discovery. doi:10.1039/d2dd00008c  arXiv:2108.02913v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2108.02913v1 (sha256 a023b9fa4ab2c2a7...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 125 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the NewtonNet method (introduced here) and its
# benchmark fits: nine MD17 molecules (Table 1), four MD17 molecules at
# CCSD/CCSD(T) accuracy (Table 2), the ANI-1 data set at 2M and 1M
# training samples (Table 3) and the methane-combustion data set at
# three training sizes (Table 4), with the hyperparameters of Table 5.
# Values are means over four random splits where the paper says so.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

