###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table 2 was read for four of its molecules (aspirin, benzene, ethanol, malonaldehyde); a fifth row (energy 0.014 kcal/mol) was cut off in the text read and is not encoded.
# - For ANI-1 the caption gives the unit as kcal/mol/atom and the text as kcal/mol; the unit is left unset and both readings are in the label. Per-atom energy errors for the methane data are in kcal/mol/atom (no unit individual).
# - Other columns (SchNet, PhysNet, DimeNet, FCHL19, sGDML, NequIP, PaiNN; ANI; DeepMD) are literature values. The hydrogen-combustion experiment listed in Table 5 was not read.
# - MD17 training-set sizes and the reference levels of MD17, ANI-1 and the methane data are not restated in the parts read. L = 3 message-passing layers, n_f = 128 features and n_b = 20 basis functions are encoded as numLayers, numFeatures and numRadialBasis; lambda_D (force-direction weight) is left out.
# - The manifest classes this paper as 'Application/model instance'; it is the originating NewtonNet method paper. Version read: arXiv v1.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
